Manfred Friedrich (mfriedrich@my-deja.com) wrote:
: Thanks for your hint. But I have no sources.

Well, if you are truly desperate to do this, having no source is
not an unsurmountable obstacle. You can always use the /proc
interface (see man 4 proc) to attach to the running process, and
intercept all it's socket() system. Upon the exit from socket(),
simply simulate setsockopt(SO_REUSEADDR) - and you are all done.

A simple matter of programming :-)

/Serge.P

